# One package per line. Installed at BUILD time with --no-install-recommends, from either the Ubuntu
# archive or a repo you added in apt/. A package that does not exist for the architecture being built
# is skipped loudly rather than failing the build, because vendor coverage on arm64 rarely matches
# amd64 and a mixed fleet still has to build.
#
# Recommends are declined deliberately. A vendor agent's Recommends can drag a desktop stack into an
# image that streams into RAM on every boot, and that shows up as a hardware requirement on every box.
#
# Examples of the kinds of thing that belong here:
#
# rsyslog          forward logs to your SIEM (configure it via rootfs/)
# ca-certificates  already in the base image, listed here only as a reminder that CA files go in rootfs/
#
# Your endpoint agent probably ships as a download rather than a repo. Put that in debs/ instead.
